WARNING:ALLOC_ARRAY_ARGS: kcalloc uses number as first arg, sizeof is generally wrong
#93: FILE: drivers/mfd/mfd-core.c:133:
+	cnts = kcalloc(sizeof(*cnts), n_devs, GFP_KERNEL);

The first argument for kcalloc or kmalloc_array should be the
number of elements.  sizeof() as the first argument is generally
wrong.

See: https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/core-api/memory-allocation.html

CHECK:UNNECESSARY_PARENTHESES: Unnecessary parentheses around 'cell->usage_count < *usage_count'
#116: FILE: drivers/mfd/mfd-core.c:159:
+	if (!*usage_count || (cell->usage_count < *usage_count))

Parentheses are not required in the following cases:

  1. Function pointer uses::

      (foo->bar)();

    could be::

      foo->bar();

  2. Comparisons in if::

      if ((foo->bar) && (foo->baz))
      if ((foo == bar))

    could be::

      if (foo->bar && foo->baz)
      if (foo == bar)

  3. addressof/dereference single Lvalues::

      &(foo->bar)
      *(foo->bar)

    could be::

      &foo->bar
      *foo->bar

